        "slc_f2ee985d9f220f98d967aec7ced696875720e334061e198e723592ac176fcb97"
      ],
      "text": "The repo defines Recursive Language Models (RLMs) as systems that keep context as symbolic state, inspect and slice it with code, call models or agents over slices, and aggregate results verifiably."
    },
    {
      "basis": "documented",
      "claim_id": "clm_96d149639f2c716d58f9ad730264ea548c90312f03a5e88148c4a9873d7e3dfd",
      "evidence_type": "organizational_statement",
      "facet": "specifications",
      "kind": "observation",
      "locators": [
        {
          "commit": "0c71127a731c33b1e2db458280aac1c4cdc254fe",
          "git_sha": "aace63030dd5d498e2f4fd5c66b96f2d7ba411fe",
          "line_end": 40,
          "line_start": 40,
          "path": "README.md",
          "repository": "rawwerks/recursive-coding-agents",
          "url": "https://github.com/rawwerks/recursive-coding-agents/blob/0c71127a731c33b1e2db458280aac1c4cdc254fe/README.md#L40-L40"
        }
      ],
      "review_state": "mechanically_checked",
      "slice_ids": [
        "slc_2762c88b1d3146c72f22d26f3ff8ede00a80959fe707afac42ccdb7a1b3614ac"
      ],
      "text": "A one-line RLM definition states the task context moves into a persistent executable environment, the root model works through handles, and final answers return through the outer model-call interface."
    },
